<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/007B">Remark <span data-tag="007B">1.5.6.3</span>.</a> In the situation of Corollary <a data-tag="007A" href="/tag/007A">1.5.6.2</a>, one can think of the simplicial set </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ Z = \operatorname{Fun}( \Delta ^2, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \underset {\operatorname{Fun}( \Lambda ^2_1, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) }{\times } \{  (g, \bullet , f) \}  \]
</div>
<p> as a “parameter space” for all choices of $2$-simplex $\sigma $ satisfying $d^{2}_0(\sigma ) = g$ and $d^{2}_2(\sigma ) = f$ (note that such $2$-simplices can be identified with the vertices of $Z$). </p>
